{"name":"Cool Vapour","hex":"#d5d7d3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cool","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a mildly low temperature.","Allowing or suggesting heat relief."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A moderate or refreshing state of cold; moderate temperature of the air between hot and cold; coolness.","A calm temperament."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cool"},{"term":"vapour","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["British standard spelling of vapor."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["British standard spelling of vapor."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vapour"}],"entries":[{"title":"Vapor","blocks":[{"text":"In physics, a vapor or vapour is a substance in the gas phase at a temperature lower than its critical temperature, which means that the vapor can be condensed to a liquid by increasing the pressure on it without reducing the temperature of the vapor. A vapor is different from an aerosol. An aerosol is a suspension of tiny particles of liquid, solid, or both within a gas."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Nitrogen_dioxide_gas.jpg/330px-Nitrogen_dioxide_gas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vapor"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Vapor_being_used_in_a_cloud_chamber.jpg/500px-Vapor_being_used_in_a_cloud_chamber.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Vapor_being_used_in_a_cloud_chamber.jpg/1280px-Vapor_being_used_in_a_cloud_chamber.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Vapor_being_used_in_a_cloud_chamber.jpg/500px-Vapor_being_used_in_a_cloud_chamber.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"If the vapor pressure exceeds the equilibrium value, it becomes supersaturated and condenses on any available nucleation sites e. g. particles of dust. This principle is used in cloud chambers, where particles of radiation are visualized because they nucleate formation of water droplets.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVapor_being_used_in_a_cloud_chamber.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Crepuscular_Rays_Beam_through_the_Mist_Blown_from_Takkakaw_Falls.jpg/500px-Crepuscular_Rays_Beam_through_the_Mist_Blown_from_Takkakaw_Falls.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Crepuscular_Rays_Beam_through_the_Mist_Blown_from_Takkakaw_Falls.jpg/1280px-Crepuscular_Rays_Beam_through_the_Mist_Blown_from_Takkakaw_Falls.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Crepuscular_Rays_Beam_through_the_Mist_Blown_from_Takkakaw_Falls.jpg/500px-Crepuscular_Rays_Beam_through_the_Mist_Blown_from_Takkakaw_Falls.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Invisible water vapor condenses to form visible water droplets called mist","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACrepuscular_Rays_Beam_through_the_Mist_Blown_from_Takkakaw_Falls.jpg"}],"sounds":{"cool":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f7/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-cool.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/f/f7/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-cool.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-cool.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/f/f7/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-cool.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-cool.wav.ogg"}]}}}